{
 "graph": {
  "name": "guitarml-ts-rat-combo",
  "version": "1.0",
  "date": "2026-10-31",
  "description": "The GuitarML Tubescreamer/Rat combo (GuitarML/GuitarPedalPCBs at e2fa7e1, TS_Rat_Combo_1590bb/jack_pedal.kicad_sch, MIT, Keith Bloemer) as published: a TS808-style stage (2SC1815 input follower, TL072 gain stage with two 1N914 in the feedback and its tone stage, 2SC1815 output follower) and a Rat-style stage (LM301A, 1N914 to ground, filter, 2N5458 source follower), a 3PDT order switch on the board, 9 V through a 1N5817; the jacks, the DC jack, the two bypass footswitches and their LEDs hang on pads – here on the hand-wired board 'wiring'. Transcribed for edakit's tests.",
  "purpose": {
   "use": "private",
   "market": "EU",
   "notes": "GuitarML publishes the boards for builders who order and build them for themselves. The transcription is a test of edakit, not a product."
  },
  "conventions": {
   "pin_reference": "'<designator>.<pin>' with the pin numbers of the parts entries – the KiCad symbols' where they agree; the 2N5458's custom symbol (1 G, 2 S, 3 D) and Device:LED (1 K, 2 A) turned into the entries' (2N5458: 1 D, 2 S, 3 G; LED: 1 A, 2 K)",
   "v": "per net: [min, max] in V over the intended operating states – 9 V from the DC jack; nets behind a coupling capacitor at ground with ±4.5 V of signal",
   "board": "main: the GuitarML PCB; wiring: the parts wired to its pads by hand (bought = true until edakit has a key for a hand-wired board)",
   "source": "GuitarML/GuitarPedalPCBs at e2fa7e1, TS_Rat_Combo_1590bb/jack_pedal.kicad_sch (checked against jack_pedal.kicad_pcb), https://github.com/GuitarML/GuitarPedalPCBs"
  },
